data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":2013,"item_id":"msg_08759bb0ca8d0470016b086b2b241087d194da8609bf5bef6e","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"wren\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The supplied related-capability searches and complete hand-bind-crossing schema establish a real gap: hand-bind-crossing@1 accepts only one wrap and has no wrap-count argument. Cord joining and cord making provide possible material preparation, not multi-wrap crossing binding. Develop a general parameterized multi-wrap operation in the current-conversation handoff, reusing the existing binding implementation rather than claiming its measurement, closure or trial mechanisms as new inventions. Previous single-wrap results establish only those recorded loads and durations; neither a longer cord nor structural capacity is established.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Develop Hand-lash crossing pieces, applicable to any actor meeting the prerequisites. Modes: attempt, inspect, trial, untie, cancel; arguments: exact pieceIds, cordId, crossingAngle, wrapCount, workId or bindingId, trialDirection, trialForce and trialDuration as applicable. Minimal implementation supports 2–4 adjacent turns, crossing angles 30–90 degrees, one continuous straight unknotted and unjoined supported fiber cord or fragment, and two owned untreated branch units. Do not bind the interface to Wren, reed item instances or 31.6 mm pieces. Unsupported material mechanics produce an explicit gap, not a fabricated result. Use hand-bind-crossing@1 for single-wrap requests rather than duplicating that function. Record code reuse of long.hand-bind-crossing / hand-bind-crossing@1, crossing-contact@1, fiber-cord@1, cord-knot@1 and cord-bend@1; implement and version only the necessary multi-wrap geometry, progress and contact extension. Dependencies are those existing measurement, cord strength, curvature, closure, wear and branch laws, plus the developed multi-turn contact solver. hand-twist-sectioned-cord and hand-join-fiber-cords remain separate existing capabilities; this operation neither makes cord nor silently accepts joined cord. Public availability establishes neither individual learning nor ownership.\\\\nPrerequisites: living actor able to grip and lift the measured pieces, sufficient energy for the next paid stage, actual reachable owned unreserved inputs, dry clear footing, room for the measured crossed pieces and nobody within the existing binding clearance of actor radius plus 1 m. Use the existing 0.1 m one-hand crossing-size limit and 100 N × health/100 lift limit. Reserve two branch units and the named cord atomically; reject invalid ownership, unavailable inputs and invalid arguments without charge. A larger lot may supply both branch units, with exact provenance retained. No tools, anchors, extra cord, helpers or new stock are supplied. Other actors are never presumed to assist, communicate or consent.\\\\nCosts: study 5 rounds at 0.2 energy per round, individually. Work has one measure-position round, one routing round per turn, one form-tuck-closure round and one dress-release-check round: wrapCount + 3 paid rounds at 0.5 energy each. Inspect takes one round at 0.2 energy; trial one round at 0.5 energy with an explicit physical hold of more than 0 and at most 60 seconds, not additional free elapsed world time; untie takes one closure-release round plus one round per turn at 0.5 energy each. Cancel costs no energy or elapsed round. Learning and work advance only through actual paid simulation rounds; development/review waiting advances nothing.\\\\nFit and mechanism: round 1 measures actual branch geometry, crossing angle, cord width, condition, available continuous length and bend limit using the cited laws. Construct an explicit collision-free centreline for each adjacent turn around both sections in the existing obtuse-bisector routing plane, including transitions between turns, finite cord width and the shared reversible overhand closure. Check hand access and bend radii throughout routing and closure formation, not just in the seated result. Required length is the maximum simultaneous occupied path over the routing/closure sequence plus required pinch lengths and tails. Reuse the existing 0.04 m routing allowance and closure opening, curvature, pinch and tail rules where applicable; do not simply multiply the single-wrap total or count a closure once per turn. Report component lengths, measured available length and shortage. The known 0.54 m cord, item-303-wren-3473, is only a possible input if actually available and adequate; its partial record is not a fit verdict. References to item-295-wren-3384 and item-287-wren-3309 in prior records identify earlier pieces, not a grant of present accessibility or availability. A paid measured shortfall records the finding and releases the unchanged inputs once.\\\\nThe smallest executable result is a hand-positioned multi-turn crossing held by the existing reversible closure, not a square-lashing strength claim or a shelter component certification. Implement explicit contact paths and tension propagation before enabling released success or loaded trials. Use cord-bend@1 closure retention and fiber-cord@1 curvature-adjusted breaking, grip, creep and damage. Release must actually retain the existing 5 N seating condition. Never multiply single-wrap holding capacity by wrapCount or assume equal load sharing. The contact extension must track individual turn tension/slack and transfer through measured contacts with the supported friction law; slipping or slack turns contribute only their actual contact. If that solver cannot yet support a configuration, permit measurement and routing as a feasible precursor and report load/release mechanics as incomplete, never held. Trial bounds remain 0 < requested force <= 10 N and 0 < duration <= 60 s, separate or slide, with existing health, grip and reachable hand-site limits. Record achieved force, duration, displacement, closure slip, turn migration, creep and damage. A pass asserts only that configuration under that trial. No load-bearing occupancy, hanging loads, shelter, general strength rating or automatic wellbeing is enabled.\\\\nConservation and progress: keep the three inputs as owned physical items; a binding is a relation with routed lengths, not a fourth material item. Preserve mass, total cord length, origin, age and condition; any break leaves accounted owned fragments and debris, not replacement cord. Store workId, actor, exact input reservations, measured route, completed paid stages, recoverable physical configuration and expenditure. Each continuation executes at most the next paid stage after rechecking conditions. Low energy, blocked room, leaving reach or an unworked round pauses without charge. Unsupported hand-held stages physically relax under the reused rules; preserve paid task progress but do not claim that loose turns remain tensioned. Resume by workId, recheck current inputs and restore relaxed routing through the necessary paid routing work before proceeding; append that work without erasing prior expenditure. No silent restart, repeated full-input reservation or duplicate product.\\\\nCancel releases unused reservations once and leaves any stable closure or loose workpiece in its actual condition; it does not automatically undo a binding. Death ends actor-driven work, releases reservations once at the actual location, and leaves any stable binding, relaxed work or fragments. Successful completion releases work reservations while preserving the binding relation and its material constraints. Paid study, measurements, work and damage are never refunded; unperformed stages are never charged. Untying requires reachable accessible closure and the existing condition-at-least-0.5 rule; failures or jams leave the actual remaining configuration and reusable progress. Unwrapping preserves cord length and existing damage, not pristine material.\\\\nOngoing state: reuse bound-cord wear of 0.0005 condition per world round once per cord, not once per turn or observation. Apply continuing relaxation and contact changes through the implemented physical rules, including while paused, without free tests or actor work. Inspect reports actual reachable state; deterioration or slip can invalidate a held state. Maintenance consists of inspection and paid untying/rebinding with suitable actual materials; no automatic repair, tension restoration or resource substitution. Enforce established eligibility, costs, conservation, progress, physical outcomes and deduplication in code rather than repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":5,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience is awarded for this request, development, learning, naming, registration, selecting a mode or mastery. The minimal implementation grants no automatic pleasure, satisfaction, comfort or nutrition effect. Actual verified personal information gain may be eligible under the existing experience system, including an honestly measured shortage or informative slip: evidence must identify actor, work/trial event, material, geometry, measured conditions and result. Functionally duplicate single-wrap facts and repeated identical trials do not become new discoveries merely because a capability or record has a different name. No new reward mechanism is required here. Any later legitimate practice benefit must be personally applicable, modest, event-backed, capped, decaying and cooldown-limited; novelty is not inherently required. Do not alter protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions; physical comfort remains capped at 10 and basic nutrition is unaffected by mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Develop reusable visual metadata from observable work and physical state, separate from function and experience: actor/work/binding IDs, exact material references, measured crossing angle, turn count, routed centreline segments, closure/tail geometry, stage, tension/slack, condition and evidence event IDs. Emit measure/shortfall, turn-routed, closure-formed, release-held or release-failed, trial-result, slip, damage/break, pause/resume/cancel and untie events only when they occur. Depict only completed physical routing, with loose, incomplete, failed and released states distinguished; incomplete contact mechanics cannot display a successful lashing or passed trial. Reuse existing branch, cord and binding render components where possible, recording reuse. No success badge, strength aura, shelter graphic, comfort icon or hidden-resource disclosure follows from study, a request, animation or an unverified outcome.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

