5 rule; failures or jams leave the actual remaining configuration and reusable progress. Unwrapping preserves cord length and existing damage, not pristine material.\\\\nOngoing state: reuse bound-cord wear of 0.0005 condition per world round once per cord, not once per turn or observation. Apply continuing relaxation and contact changes through the implemented physical rules, including while paused, without free tests or actor work. Inspect reports actual reachable state; deterioration or slip can invalidate a held state. Maintenance consists of inspection and paid untying/rebinding with suitable actual materials; no automatic repair, tension restoration or resource substitution. Enforce established eligibility, costs, conservation, progress, physical outcomes and deduplication in code rather than repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":5,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience is awarded for this request, development, learning, naming, registration, selecting a mode or mastery. The minimal implementation grants no automatic pleasure, satisfaction, comfort or nutrition effect. Actual verified personal information gain may be eligible under the existing experience system, including an honestly measured shortage or informative slip: evidence must identify actor, work/trial event, material, geometry, measured conditions and result. Functionally duplicate single-wrap facts and repeated identical trials do not become new discoveries merely because a capability or record has a different name. No new reward mechanism is required here. Any later legitimate practice benefit must be personally applicable, modest, event-backed, capped, decaying and cooldown-limited; novelty is not inherently required. Do not alter protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions; physical comfort remains capped at 10 and basic nutrition is unaffected by mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Develop reusable visual metadata from observable work and physical state, separate from function and experience: actor/work/binding IDs, exact material references, measured crossing angle, turn count, routed centreline segments, closure/tail geometry, stage, tension/slack, condition and evidence event IDs. Emit measure/shortfall, turn-routed, closure-formed, release-held or release-failed, trial-result, slip, damage/break, pause/resume/cancel and untie events only when they occur. Depict only completed physical routing, with loose, incomplete, failed and released states distinguished; incomplete contact mechanics cannot display a successful lashing or passed trial. Reuse existing branch, cord and binding render components where possible, recording reuse. No success badge, strength aura, shelter graphic, comfort icon or hidden-resource disclosure follows from study, a request, animation or an unverified outcome.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}}

